---
import DocumentLayout from '../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import { pages } from '../data/pages';
---

<DocumentLayout
  title="Disclaimer"
  description="Understand the practical limits behind the previews and pixels."
  eyebrow="UPDATED OCTOBER 27, 2026"
  metaTitle={pages.disclaimer.metaTitle}
  metaDescription={pages.disclaimer.metaDescription}
>
  <h2>Review the actual result</h2>
  <p>
    Image utilities support everyday editing, not a guarantee of photographic
    fidelity, confidentiality, or acceptance by a third-party platform. Check
    the generated file’s appearance, dimensions, size, format, and available
    metadata before publishing it.
  </p>
  <h2>Quality and format differences</h2>
  <p>
    Browser decoding and encoding can change color rendering, metadata, file
    size, and pixel representation. JPEG has no transparency. Canvas WebP
    quality is not a true lossless-mode guarantee. PNG cannot recreate detail
    lost in an earlier lossy image. Enlarging an image does not reconstruct
    original detail.
  </p>
  <h2>Targets and presets</h2>
  <p>
    A requested file size is an optimization goal and may not be achievable with
    the permitted settings. The interface reports actual bytes and target
    failure. Social image recommendations can change; presets distinguish linked
    verified recommendations from general starting canvases. Confirm safe areas,
    account-specific rules, and actual placement behavior separately.
  </p>
  <h2>Privacy is broader than metadata</h2>
  <p>
    Local processing avoids sending image input as part of the core operation.
    It does not protect against compromised devices, browser extensions,
    clipboard history, screenshots, or identifying content visible in an image.
    Canvas re-encoding does not prove anonymity.
  </p>
  <h2>Independent utility</h2>
  <p>
    PixelTools is not affiliated with the social platforms, browser projects, or
    hosting services referenced in its documentation. AdSense preparation is not
    site approval. Performance targets are only measured scores where a report
    explicitly says so.
  </p>
  <p>
    See the <a href="/terms">Terms of Use</a> and each tool’s guide for its
    supported behavior.
  </p>
</DocumentLayout>
